quotes.quote:
A safe rename uses this ProtoJSON request body:

```json
{
  "campaign": {
    "name": "campaigns/C7",
    "displayName": "Summer"
  },
  "updateMask": "displayName"
}
```

Its **expected stored resource**, derived from the contract and starting from the supplied original state, is:

```json
{
  "name": "campaigns/C7",
  "displayName": "Summer",
  "description": "Approved",
  "spendLimitMicros": "25000000"
}
```

The mask is a ProtoJSON string with resource-relative, lower-camel-case paths. `name` identifies the campaign; it is not a mutable field or part of this mask.

An intentional description reset, starting **independently from the original before-state**, is:

```json
{
  "campaign": {
    "name": "campaigns/C7",
    "description": ""
  },
  "updateMask": "description"
}
```

Its **expected stored resource** is:

```json
{
  "name": "campaigns/C7",
  "displayName": "Spring",
  "description": "",
  "spendLimitMicros": "25000000"
}
```

Under this particular contract, selecting `description` also resets it when its value is absent from the normalized message. Thus serializer omission of the empty string can still produce the intended reset **with that explicit mask**. Omitting the mask would also select and reset the other mutable fields.
